  "notes": "Herdr fork preview (wwelder/herdr): the priority sort orders each status by last activity time\n\nSource: 38850e26bf312ecd729e388e6cc5af49463c34d3.\n\n- With `agent_panel_sort = \"priority\"`, agents of the same status are ordered by when each last did something, latest first, on one machine and across saved machines alike. The time comes from a `last_active` metadata token in unix seconds, which the agent's host reports (the `herdr-ago` ticker sets it next to `$ago`). It replaces the order of state changes, which started over in pane order whenever a server or client restarted. Agents without a report keep the old order, after those with one. Working agents keep the state-change order. A folded subagent group sits where its caller's row belongs. Client-only: restart the client to see it.\n\nAll five assets were built by the manual Build artifacts workflow (run 45299396016).\n\nUpdate with `herdr update` on the preview channel.",
